wrong word. The two real surfaces:

  * kicad_routing_plugin/gui_utils.py -- run_kicad_oracle_on_live_board never
    inspected `available`, so an oracle that COULD NOT RUN was byte-identical
    here to one that ran and found everything connected: both an empty results
    dict, both silent. It now says the clean result is UNBACKED. This is a
    changed line in kicad_routing_plugin/, which the previous entry could
    record as "ZERO changed lines".
  * py_router/kicad_parser.py _live_fill -- the GUI's exact_fill_provider. Its
    LOUD stale-clearance warning fired only from `except`, so a refill that
    RETURNED nothing (a 300 s timeout above all) fell through to the in-process
    fill in silence, on the routing WORKER thread. Both arrivals now share one
    warning function.

